{"kelime":"هندباء","sozlukler":{"kaikki_vikisozluk":[{"w":"هندباء","u":"هندباء","p":"noun","t":"From Aramaic הּנְדְּבָא / ܗܶܢܕܒܳܐ (hendǝḇā), cognate to Arabic هَدَب (hadab, “twisted leaves or sprigs; cilium”). From Semitic also Medieval Greek ἔντυβον (éntubon), whence reborrowed Classical Syriac ܐܢܛܘܒܝܐ (anṭūbiyā, “endive, dandelion, chicory”) and the European terms Late Latin intibus, English endive etc.","s":[["bor","Aramaic הּנְדְּבָא"],["cog","Arabic"],["doublet","هَدَب (hadab, “twisted leaves or sprigs; cilium”)"],["cog","Semitic"],["cog","Medieval Greek ἔντυβον (éntubon)"],["cog","Classical Syriac ܐܢܛܘܒܝܐ (anṭūbiyā, “endive, dandelion, chicory”)"],["cog","Late Latin intibus"],["cog","English endive"]],"g":["dandelion (Taraxacum gen.)","chicory, endive (Cichorium gen.)"],"tag":["collective"],"r":["hindibāʔ"],"ipa":["/hin.di.baːʔ/"],"ds":[["axm","հնդիպայ","hndipay"],["axm","հնդիպէ","hndipē"],["az","hindiba",""],["ota","هندبا","hindiba"]],"el":[["הּנְדְּבָא","הנדבא#Aramaic"],["ܗܶܢܕܒܳܐ","ܗܢܕܒܐ#Classical_Syriac"],["هَدَب","هدب#Arabic"],["ἔντυβον","ἔντυβον#Ancient_Greek"],["ܐܢܛܘܒܝܐ","ܐܢܛܘܒܝܐ#Classical_Syriac"],["intibus","intibus#Latin"],["endive","endive#English"]],"yol":""}]}}